  message: "[REVIEW 2026-11-15: REAL TODAY, TEXT PARTLY STALE] 2026-11-15, dev e2b6ab8096 (stable-id v14). Reproduces: `pub const N: u32 = 1;` -> `rust:src/lib.rs:1-1:N:variable`. The arm is rust.py:1668, shared by `const_item` and `static_item`. Pinned tally unchanged: 150 paired, 135 agree, 15 `constant` vs `variable`. Token facts: the registry has both `constant` (symbol_kinds.py:231) and `const` (:233); the SCIP arm emits `constant` (scip/index.py:241), so only `constant` gives 0 disagreements. No mainstream analyzer emits either token for a const (C++/JS/TS/Kotlin emit `variable`; only julia and thrift emit `const`, tlaplus `constant`). SCIP maps statics to `variable`. Scheme bumps v11-v14 shipped since filing without this. Full review: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/reports/WI-zigup.md. No status or priority change made by this review."  # 3d64
